From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:17:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Control channel: connections must authenticate within 10 s
 (backport)

Backport of upstream 64520f645e073b23960b774a677d54f504094843 (#5229),
automation crate only.

The AROS build of photocraft-cli includes `serve --port`, the headless
loopback JSON control server (std::net, not the Tokio bridge), so this
path ships even though the TCP MCP bridge does not. Before this change an
unauthenticated connection was limited only by the 30 s idle timeout,
which restarts with every read: sixteen clients trickling bytes could hold
every connection permit. AuthDeadlineStream fails reads once 10 s have
passed since connecting until `auth` succeeds.

Not taken: apps/photocraft/src/control_server.rs (the desktop eframe app's
listener, not built for AROS; the AROS shell has no control listener).
The import list keeps this base's names (no repeat_auth_reply here).
